      {
        "id": 131686,
        "name": "Pulseglazer",
        "username": "Pulseglazer",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/p/f04885/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2015-02-20T18:35:39.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Yes, but since you used Wraith as an example, Stealth until she’s set up is generally better than the other options.  When she has everything out, her surviving longer or shrugging off the first big hit that comes her way has value.</p>\n<p>That, to me, is the problem with the Expat promo. Neither it nor her base power are any use if you cant find a gun. I’ve gone two or three turns with no gun. It is not fun.  My wife, meanwhile, always gets the shotgun by turn 2.</p>\n<p>Finally, Bunker is the perfect example of how to handle this. Is his 3 points or so of power damage worth more than DR on a negative 2 damage villain? Is foregoing that damage worth getting rid of a nasty ongoing? Both yes, right?  That added utility from the powers is just perfect.</p>",
